{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfryi2CuF2HPv83CoACpf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The export module is now a plugin registry. The three formats live in `export/formats/`, and `core.py` contains no format logic. All 10 tests pass: the 5 original ones and 5 new ones. I did not commit anything.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`export/registry.py`** (new): `Exporter` ABC with `name`, `extension`, and `dump(records)`. It also has `register(cls)` as a class decorator, `get(name)`, `names()`, and `UnknownFormat`. Registering a name twice raises `ValueError`.\n- **`export/formats/`** (new): `csv.py`, `json.py`, and `xml.py`, each a registered `Exporter` subclass. The output logic is copied unchanged from the old if-chains.\n- **`export/formats/__init__.py`**: imports every module in the package with `pkgutil`, so the decorators run when `import export` is executed. A new format is a new file in that directory.\n- **`export/core.py`**: `export_records` and `export_to_file` keep their signatures and now delegate to `get(fmt)`. They contain no format names.\n- **`export/__init__.py`**: still exports `export_records`, `export_to_file`, and `UnknownFormat`. It also exposes `Exporter`, `register`, `get`, and `names`.\n- **`tests/test_registry.py`** (new): covers built-in names, the unknown-format message for both functions, a plugin added with no `core.py` change, and duplicate rejection. The plugin test swaps the registry dict with `monkeypatch`, so it does not leak into other tests.\n\n**Choices I made that you may want to change**\n\n- `get(name)` returns a registered instance, not the class.\n- `extension` keeps the leading dot (`\".csv\"`), matching the old `_extension` helper, so `export_to_file` behaviour is unchanged.\n- The unknown-format message reads `unknown format 'yaml'; known formats: csv, json, xml`. Names are sorted.\n- The format modules are named `csv.py`, `json.py`, and `xml.py`. Imports are absolute, so they resolve to the stdlib modules. The risk is only if someone runs a script from inside `export/formats/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8084,"cache_read_input_tokens":55456,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8084},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9790712c-1cf5-4579-8d47-c89dd4901fd1","uuid":"4758b843-d6a4-4629-bf83-fe0a55ed47db","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:28:13.865Z","request_id":"req_011Cfryi1wHFgXTXpmpYsptm"}
